# Resource Request Form — authentication (BE-00 · OBT-464)
#
# This product has no login of its own: it uses the shared /api/auth with the
# app_key below. What belongs to it are the app_key and the three roles —
# equipe, mesa, gestor — seeded by scripts/seed_apps_roles.py.
#
# Before running: apply the seed, then grant a role to the test account.
#   uv run python scripts/seed_apps_roles.py
#   uv run python scripts/grant_app_role.py mesa.local@test.com resource-request-form mesa

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@appKey = resource-request-form

### Signup — the mesa test account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mesa.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "display_name": "Mesa Local"
}

### Signup — a second account, deliberately left without a role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sempapel.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "display_name": "Sem Papel"
}

### Login — run this first; the token feeds the calls below
# @name rrf_login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mesa.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Me
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{rrf_login.response.body.tokens.access_token}}

### My roles for this app — the call FE-24 makes to hydrate a session
# Expected: [{ "app_key": "resource-request-form", "role_key": "mesa" }]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/my-roles?app_key={{appKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rrf_login.response.body.tokens.access_token}}

### Login as the account with no role
# @name rrf_login_norole
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sempapel.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### My roles for the account with no role — expected: []
# An empty array, not a 403: my-roles reports, it does not guard. What refuses is
# require_app_access on the module's own routes — and the module has none yet,
# because routes are BE-02/BE-03. The 403 is proven in
# tests/test_resource_requests/test_access.py, against a probe router.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/my-roles?app_key={{appKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rrf_login_norole.response.body.tokens.access_token}}

### Forgot password — the FE-25 email
# The app_key is what points the link at this product: request_password_reset
# looks the row up in `apps` and builds {app_url}/reset-password?token=…
# app_url is https://resourceform.shemaywam.com.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mesa.local@test.com",
  "app_key": "resource-request-form"
}

### Reset password — token comes from the email above
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL",
  "password": "novasenha123"
}
